Make tray SNI and DBusMenu responses type-correct.

This is the full diff of upstream PR #152
(<https://github.com/ProtonVPN/proton-vpn-gtk-app/pull/152>):

- DBusMenu GetLayout children become spec-conformant `av` (array of
  variants), via the new `_empty_layout_children` / `_layout_item_properties`
  helpers and `dbus.Struct(child_layout)` appended to a `signature="v"`
  array. Without this, strict tray hosts like HyprPanel's astal-tray
  segfault on the first menu read with:

    GLib-CRITICAL: format string '(i@a{sv}@av)' has type '(ia{sv}av)'
    but value has type '(ia{sv}a(ia{sv}av))'

- Separator menu entries no longer carry `label`/`enabled` keys, only
  `type` and `visible`. Some hosts (HyprPanel) draw separators with a
  thicker style when the dict carries label/enabled fields it doesn't
  expect there.

- StatusNotifierItem `Get` and `GetAll` now share `_get_sni_properties`
  and emit the full standard SNI property table (`IconPixmap`,
  `OverlayIconName`, `ToolTip`, `WindowId`, …) with correct types, so
  hosts that probe these via `Get` no longer get raw strings/None back.

Tracking: PR #152 was rebased on `stable` at proton-vpn v4.16.1 to
clear merge conflicts; the diff still applies cleanly to v4.15.3 which
nixpkgs currently ships. Drop this patch + the proton-vpn override
once #152 lands and the new package reaches nixpkgs.

